      "evidence": "design.md 'No mergeability': 'GitHub `mergeable` is not read.' The only code changes are in `_prepare` (publication_queue.py, the `RederivationEnvironmentFailed` handler calling `merge_conflicts`) and in the `_integrate` environment-note path. The tests mock merge-tree and no test covers a mergeable=CONFLICTING input. The case where merge-tree is clean and `mergeable` is CONFLICTING gets only the reason text from the environment note, with no routing to integration-repair.",
      "id": "conflict-signal-ignores-github-mergeable",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "Requirement item 3 is phrased around GitHub reporting mergeable=CONFLICTING. The change never reads that signal. It relies only on the queue's own git merge-tree in `_prepare`. A PR that GitHub marks CONFLICTING but merge-tree reports clean would still stay in blocked-retryable, and the only evidence is the environment note."
